The reviewed r8 controller captured the complete tracked-path write barrier:
669 Application entries and 210 Control entries. The resulting canonical JSON
was 236,582 bytes. Its writer had no conflicting bound, while the generic
private-JSON reader and guarded-release file check retained a 131,072-byte
ceiling. The first read therefore rejected the journal immediately after its
durable publication, before backup or repository mutation.

The r9 correction assigns only the authenticated barrier journal a 1 MiB
ceiling. Other private JSON artifacts retain their existing 128 KiB bound.
The journal writer measures the exact canonical ASCII representation before
publication and rejects an oversized payload without replacing the current
journal. Existing schema, root ownership, mode 0600, single-link, duplicate-key
and exact metadata validation remain fail-closed.

R8 remains immutable and is not retried. Recovery of the pristine r8 orphan
journal and any subsequent runtime attempt require the reviewed r9 controller,
new Same-SHA review, merge, CI and a distinct immutable freeze.
